title: the wholesale-wipe guard only catches an empty remote, not a swapped one
updated: 2026-08-10T04:50:23Z
---

Follow-up to #82, stated by the fix rather than found after it.

pull now refuses to reconcile when the plan would leave zero board refs, and
rolls the tracking mirror back before refusing, so "the remote is empty for the
wrong reason" no longer wipes the board. accept_wipe / karr sync --prune is the
deliberate way through.

What is still not caught: a remote that was replaced by a DIFFERENT non-empty
board. Point karr at the wrong origin -- a stale clone, a fresh board someone
else init-ed at the same URL, a typo in the remote -- and reconciliation treats
it as the truth and converges the local board onto it. The zero-ref check does
not fire because the ref count is not zero.

A board identity would fix it properly: stamp something durable at init
(refs/karr/meta/board-id), compare it on pull, and refuse when the remote board
is a different one than the local board was last reconciled against. That also
gives a clean answer for the empty case -- absent id plus zero refs is a fresh
remote, absent id plus refs is a foreign board.

Not urgent while everyone points at one remote, but the failure is silent and
total, which is the same property that made #82 worth fixing.
Geschlossen durch 9f03821 + Merge: board-id in refs/karr/meta/board-id, Vergleich vor jeder Reconciliation, Refusal mit Mirror-Rollback; --accept-foreign-board ist der bewusste Weg. Migration: Bestandsboards werden beim ersten Pull gestempelt. t/99 + t/104.
